WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.047 --> 00:00:03.483
[door opens]

2
00:00:03.613 --> 00:00:06.529
[ominous music]

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:13.667
♪ ♪

4
00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.790
[screaming] No!

5
00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:51.705
Oh. my God! Oh. God!
No! Please!

6
00:00:51.792 --> 00:00:53.533
- Shh! Enough!
- Ah! No. please!

7
00:00:53.663 --> 00:00:54.751
- Just behave!
- No!

8
00:00:54.795 --> 00:00:58.668
[screaming]

9
00:00:58.755 --> 00:00:59.669
Damn it!

10
00:00:59.756 --> 00:01:01.410
[panting]

11
00:01:01.497 --> 00:01:02.977
Ow!

12
00:01:03.108 --> 00:01:04.892
What the hell. Alice? Oh.

13
00:01:04.979 --> 00:01:06.024
Damn it. Josh!

14
00:01:06.154 --> 00:01:07.460
- Stay in character!
- Well. I'm sorry!

15
00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:08.547
I just didn't expect you
to get so rough!

16
00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.810
Is my nose bleeding?

17
00:01:09.897 --> 00:01:11.551
- Ugh. no. it is not bleeding.
- Damn it.

18
00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.682
It's definitely gonna bruise.

19
00:01:12.813 --> 00:01:13.988
I have to present
to clients on Monday.

20
00:01:14.075 --> 00:01:14.989
This was a stupid idea.
Let's just forget it.

21
00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.382
No. no.
Wait. wait. wait. wait.

22
00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:17.773
I've got this.
Let me try again.

23
00:01:17.904 --> 00:01:19.994
[owl hooting]

24
00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:22.127
I'm gonna ravage you.

25
00:01:22.257 --> 00:01:23.563
Gross.

26
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.477
Well. I'm sorry.

27
00:01:24.564 --> 00:01:26.522
Do not apologize.

28
00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:27.741
[distant scream]

29
00:01:27.784 --> 00:01:30.396
♪

30
00:01:30.439 --> 00:01:31.874
It came from Susan's house.

31
00:01:31.963 --> 00:01:33.573
- Call 911.
- Josh. no.

32
00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.660
Let the cops handle it.

33
00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:35.967
Just stay here. okay?

34
00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:37.229
[phone beeps]

35
00:01:37.316 --> 00:01:44.410
♪ ♪

36
00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:48.327
Susan?

37
00:01:48.414 --> 00:01:49.632
Susan!

38
00:01:51.765 --> 00:01:53.374
Are you all right?

39
00:02:01.427 --> 00:02:03.559
If there's anybody in here.

40
00:02:03.603 --> 00:02:05.300
cops are on the way!

41
00:02:05.431 --> 00:02:12.133
♪ ♪

42
00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:23.840
♪ ♪

43
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:30.125
Susan Granwell.
dead in the kitchen.

44
00:02:30.212 --> 00:02:31.692
Must have been a pretty
big donor for the mayor

45
00:02:31.779 --> 00:02:32.998
to ask you all to step in.

46
00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:35.130
They were old friends.
What do we know?

47
00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:37.219
Neighbors heard a commotion
around 11:00 p.m.

48
00:02:37.306 --> 00:02:39.265
One of them came
to check on Susan.

49
00:02:39.308 --> 00:02:42.007
found her bleeding out on
the ground. already deceased.

50
00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.226
Preliminary cause of death is
blunt force trauma to the head.

51
00:02:44.313 --> 00:02:46.620
Looks like she got hit
with that cast iron.

52
00:02:46.663 --> 00:02:48.535
Okay. we'll have it sent to
the lab for further processing.

53
00:02:48.665 --> 00:02:49.579
Whose firearm is that?

54
00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:51.538
Registered to the victim.

55
00:02:51.625 --> 00:02:53.583
but CSU didn't recover
any shell casings.

56
00:02:53.714 --> 00:02:56.151
So she wasn't able to fire
it off before she got hit.

57
00:02:56.238 --> 00:02:57.849
That skillet's
a weapon of opportunity.

58
00:02:57.892 --> 00:02:59.372
so it's not premeditated murder.

59
00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:00.677
What. a robbery gone wrong?

60
00:03:00.808 --> 00:03:02.549
She confronted them with a gun.

61
00:03:02.679 --> 00:03:04.029
they retaliated
by grabbing a cast iron?

62
00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:05.378
Maybe.

63
00:03:05.508 --> 00:03:07.249
Nice house. lots of valuables.

64
00:03:07.336 --> 00:03:08.685
Doesn't feel like a break-in.

65
00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:10.905
Only disturbance was in here.

66
00:03:10.992 --> 00:03:13.168
Windows and doors were intact.
Alarm didn't go.

67
00:03:13.255 --> 00:03:14.866
Whoever did this
either had access to the house.

68
00:03:14.909 --> 00:03:17.346
or she let them in.

69
00:03:17.477 --> 00:03:19.740
Looks like a crime of passion.

70
00:03:19.783 --> 00:03:23.135
I have a feeling Susan Granwell
knew her killer.

71
00:03:23.222 --> 00:03:25.050
All right. folks.
last night. Susan Granwell

72
00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:27.399
was attacked and killed
in her home.

73
00:03:27.443 --> 00:03:31.143
a $12 million historically
preserved home in Fieldston.

74
00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.842
Susan was a major donor
and confidant of the mayor.

75
00:03:34.929 --> 00:03:37.845
He would like her killer
brought to justice immediately.

76
00:03:37.976 --> 00:03:39.325
Right. hey. have we
notified the family yet?

77
00:03:39.412 --> 00:03:41.718
No... her son Bobby is in Tokyo
with his grandparents.

78
00:03:41.762 --> 00:03:42.762
and because of the time change.

79
00:03:42.894 --> 00:03:44.373
we haven't been able
to reach them.

80
00:03:44.504 --> 00:03:46.549
But by the time I have to
look this boy in the eyes

81
00:03:46.636 --> 00:03:47.855
and tell him his mother is gone.

82
00:03:47.986 --> 00:03:49.683
I would like to have
some real answers for him.

83
00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.859
Our team's initial
assessment was that

84
00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.992
this looks like
a crime of passion.

85
00:03:54.122 --> 00:03:55.994
so let's talk about
Susan Granwell and anyone

86
00:03:56.081 --> 00:03:57.734
in her life who could have
snapped and killed her.

87
00:03:57.821 --> 00:03:58.997
Right. well. Susan grew up

88
00:03:59.084 --> 00:04:01.042
an Upper East Side socialite.
old money.

89
00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:03.392
Now she's a hotelier
by way of marriage.

90
00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:05.699
Her late husband. Alex. founded
a chain of boutique hotels

91
00:04:05.786 --> 00:04:07.222
called the Granwell Hotels.

92
00:04:07.309 --> 00:04:08.267
They have locations
across the country.

93
00:04:08.354 --> 00:04:09.746
Yeah. Sam and I stayed
at a Granwell once.

94
00:04:09.877 --> 00:04:11.183
They had a pillow menu.

95
00:04:11.313 --> 00:04:12.793
Well. that's not all they got.

96
00:04:12.836 --> 00:04:14.447
Turns out Granwell Hotels
is knee-deep

97
00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:15.969
in a serious labor dispute.

98
00:04:16.057 --> 00:04:17.450
Maintenance
and hospitality workers

99
00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.540
have been on strike
for the past three months

100
00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.237
with no end in sight.

101
00:04:22.281 --> 00:04:23.935
They claim Susan is
trying to starve them out.

102
00:04:24.022 --> 00:04:25.501
The protests have been peaceful.

103
00:04:25.588 --> 00:04:26.763
but it's getting nasty.

104
00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.852
Nasty enough to attack
Susan in her own home?

105
00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.028
She thought so.

106
00:04:30.158 --> 00:04:31.899
Susan filed a police report
last week

107
00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.901
after a brick was thrown
through her front window.

108
00:04:34.032 --> 00:04:35.859
She blamed her
disgruntled employees.

109
00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.036
but the cops weren't able
to ID a suspect.

110
00:04:38.079 --> 00:04:39.733
So the brick was to
scare her into returning

111
00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.691
to the negotiating table.

112
00:04:41.778 --> 00:04:43.737
When that didn't work. maybe
they amped up the intimidation.

113
00:04:43.824 --> 00:04:45.434
and it got out of hand.

114
00:04:45.478 --> 00:04:46.914
Who's running this union?

115
00:04:47.045 --> 00:04:48.698
That would be Jeremy Payton.

116
00:04:48.785 --> 00:04:50.352
career labor organizer.

117
00:04:50.439 --> 00:04:52.180
known for running
campaigns of intimidation.

118
00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.877
He has threatened multiple times

119
00:04:54.008 --> 00:04:55.270
to burn down
Granwell properties.

120
00:04:55.401 --> 00:04:57.011
Not the type to catch
flies with honey. huh?

121
00:04:57.142 --> 00:04:58.970
Definitely not.

122
00:04:59.057 --> 00:05:03.670
Granwell sent their goons
to rough me up. to silence me.

123
00:05:03.713 --> 00:05:05.802
We're not scared of you!

124
00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:07.587
You hear that. Susan?

125
00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:09.719
You should be scared of us!

126
00:05:09.806 --> 00:05:11.808
Well. he might be a charmer.
but if it walks like a motive

127
00:05:11.939 --> 00:05:12.940
and talks like a motive...

128
00:05:13.027 --> 00:05:14.376
Well. forensics
might back it up.

129
00:05:14.463 --> 00:05:15.856
Yeah?

130
00:05:15.899 --> 00:05:17.336
Report from the crime scene
just landed.

131
00:05:17.466 --> 00:05:19.164
and Jeremy's fingerprints
were found all over it.

132
00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:20.687
- Mm.
- Low lipid oxidation

133
00:05:20.817 --> 00:05:23.037
in the residue suggests
his prints were recent.

134
00:05:23.124 --> 00:05:24.604
- What about the murder weapon?
- Wiped clean.

135
00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:25.692
No fingerprints there.

136
00:05:25.779 --> 00:05:27.128
Well. nice try. Jeremy.

137
00:05:27.215 --> 00:05:28.521
The man was there.

138
00:05:28.608 --> 00:05:32.046
Let's bring him in.

139
00:05:32.177 --> 00:05:35.310
all: Granwell. Granwell.
you can't hide!

140
00:05:35.397 --> 00:05:37.965
We can see your greedy side!

141
00:05:38.052 --> 00:05:40.968
Granwell. Granwell.
you can't hide!

142
00:05:41.055 --> 00:05:42.709
We can see your greedy side!
- Back up. scabs!

143
00:05:42.752 --> 00:05:45.277
Nobody's getting through
this picket line!

144
00:05:45.407 --> 00:05:47.148
Get out of here! Boo!

145
00:05:47.235 --> 00:05:48.758
Scab!

146
00:05:48.845 --> 00:05:50.673
Scab!

147
00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:51.848
- Excuse me. FBI.
Excuse us.

148
00:05:51.892 --> 00:05:54.764
[indistinct shouting]

149
00:05:54.851 --> 00:05:57.071
Jeremy Payton. how you doing?
FBI.

150
00:05:57.158 --> 00:05:58.551
Why don't we take the
temperature down a little bit?

151
00:05:58.681 --> 00:06:02.511
Law enforcement protecting
the corporate fat cats again!

152
00:06:02.642 --> 00:06:04.774
Why am I not surprised?

153
00:06:04.861 --> 00:06:06.037
No. No. wait.

154
00:06:06.124 --> 00:06:08.126
That's not what's
happening here. okay?

155
00:06:08.169 --> 00:06:09.866
Look. Mr. Payton. we have
a few questions for you.

156
00:06:09.953 --> 00:06:13.435
so why don't you come with us?

157
00:06:13.566 --> 00:06:15.655
Obstructing a federal agent
is a crime. fellas.

158
00:06:15.785 --> 00:06:18.092
So move. Now.

159
00:06:18.179 --> 00:06:20.312
Oh. you don't tell them
what to do. sweetheart.

160
00:06:20.442 --> 00:06:21.530
Sweetheart?

161
00:06:21.661 --> 00:06:22.531
Okay. yeah. no.
that's not gonna work.

162
00:06:22.618 --> 00:06:24.011
Let's go.

163
00:06:24.098 --> 00:06:25.447
You two. step aside.
or you're coming.

164
00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:26.666
Let's go.
Hands behind your back.

165
00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:29.234
See? You see
what they're doing to us?

166
00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:32.324
Don't let these jackboots
take away your voices!

167
00:06:32.454 --> 00:06:34.021
Union strong!

168
00:06:34.108 --> 00:06:35.718
all: Union strong!

169
00:06:35.805 --> 00:06:36.979
Union strong!

170
00:06:37.068 --> 00:06:38.721
Union strong!

171
00:06:38.808 --> 00:06:40.201
You hear that. Susan?

172
00:06:40.288 --> 00:06:41.724
You should be scared...

173
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.468
From the moment I saw you guys.

174
00:06:46.555 --> 00:06:47.991
I knew that this was
what it was about.

175
00:06:48.079 --> 00:06:49.602
That's not what
you were screaming

176
00:06:49.689 --> 00:06:51.082
at your union brethren about.

177
00:06:51.169 --> 00:06:52.779
You wanted them to believe
that we were there

178
00:06:52.866 --> 00:06:54.259
to shut down your picket.

179
00:06:54.346 --> 00:06:57.131
I saw an opportunity
to keep my people angry.

180
00:06:57.175 --> 00:06:59.133
energized. and I took it.

181
00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.482
Sure. it was theater.

182
00:07:00.613 --> 00:07:03.181
but so was this.

183
00:07:03.268 --> 00:07:05.313
Nothing I said
on that video was real.

184
00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:06.706
So Granwell Hotels
never sent you

185
00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.142
their people to beat you up?

186
00:07:08.186 --> 00:07:10.362
Not physically. but you know.

187
00:07:10.449 --> 00:07:11.928
they've been beating us down
for long enough.

188
00:07:12.059 --> 00:07:13.800
Jeremy. please. stop.

189
00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.281
All right? That's enough.

190
00:07:16.368 --> 00:07:17.804
Did you fake these injuries.

191
00:07:17.891 --> 00:07:20.023
file a false police report

192
00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:21.982
blaming Susan Granwell's
private security?

193
00:07:22.025 --> 00:07:24.506
You gotta give them an enemy
to keep them motivated.

194
00:07:24.593 --> 00:07:27.509
So yeah. I had a couple
of my boys rough me up.

195
00:07:27.596 --> 00:07:28.989
Blamed it all on management.

196
00:07:29.076 --> 00:07:30.686
Sounds like a felony.

197
00:07:30.773 --> 00:07:32.862
Well. it worked.

198
00:07:32.949 --> 00:07:34.212
Momentum's on our side now.

199
00:07:34.299 --> 00:07:36.736
So if Susan Granwell is losing.

200
00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.216
why'd you pay her a visit?

201
00:07:38.303 --> 00:07:40.696
Your fingerprints.
they're all over Susan's home.

202
00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.002
[scoffs]

203
00:07:42.045 --> 00:07:44.570
Doorknobs. kitchen counters.

204
00:07:44.657 --> 00:07:48.008
Question is. are we gonna
find them on Susan's body?

205
00:07:48.095 --> 00:07:49.401
Hold up. her body?

206
00:07:49.531 --> 00:07:51.185
- You killed her.
- Wait. I...

207
00:07:51.272 --> 00:07:53.100
Beat her to death
and then fled. did you not?

208
00:07:53.187 --> 00:07:54.667
- Whoa...
what are you talking about?

209
00:07:54.753 --> 00:07:56.059
No. no. no. no. no. I didn't...

210
00:07:56.147 --> 00:07:57.800
[tense music]

211
00:07:57.931 --> 00:07:58.845
What? No.

212
00:07:58.932 --> 00:08:00.586
No. no. Susie.

213
00:08:00.673 --> 00:08:01.369
That's my Susie.

214
00:08:03.023 --> 00:08:04.024
Your Susie?

215
00:08:04.155 --> 00:08:06.244
- I didn't do this.
I would never.

216
00:08:06.287 --> 00:08:07.810
I mean. we... we couldn't
come out publicly.

217
00:08:07.941 --> 00:08:09.072
but we were in love.

218
00:08:09.203 --> 00:08:11.249
This woman was your sworn enemy.

219
00:08:11.336 --> 00:08:12.685
You trash talked her daily.

220
00:08:12.772 --> 00:08:14.513
For show.

221
00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.951
From the second we met at
negotiations. I felt a spark.

222
00:08:18.038 --> 00:08:21.084
We... we were the same. stubborn.

223
00:08:21.128 --> 00:08:23.043
We wanted big things. you know?

224
00:08:23.174 --> 00:08:24.784
We just chose different paths.

225
00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:27.352
But that didn't stop the fates
from bringing us together.

226
00:08:27.439 --> 00:08:30.006
It's a good story. but you know.

227
00:08:30.093 --> 00:08:31.791
you've also proven
that you're a good actor.

228
00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:32.835
It's not acting.

229
00:08:32.965 --> 00:08:34.315
Prove it.

230
00:08:34.402 --> 00:08:36.926
♪ ♪

231
00:08:37.013 --> 00:08:39.059
I proposed. How about that?

232
00:08:40.669 --> 00:08:43.802
With my nan's heirloom ring.

233
00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.718
[crying] You can check
the pics on my cell phone.

234
00:08:45.805 --> 00:08:47.198
There's proof there.

235
00:08:47.241 --> 00:08:49.461
I didn't do this!

236
00:08:49.591 --> 00:08:51.158
I...

237
00:08:51.245 --> 00:08:52.464
[door beeps. opens]

238
00:08:52.551 --> 00:08:56.032
♪ ♪

239
00:08:56.119 --> 00:08:56.990
Hey. Take a look at that.

240
00:08:58.861 --> 00:09:00.298
Happy family.

241
00:09:00.385 --> 00:09:01.255
Doesn't mean he's innocent.
though.

242
00:09:01.386 --> 00:09:02.909
No. but his alibi does.

243
00:09:03.039 --> 00:09:04.606
The JOC confirmed
via security cams

244
00:09:04.693 --> 00:09:05.999
that Jeremy was at
the union office

245
00:09:06.086 --> 00:09:07.087
at the time of the murder.

246
00:09:07.218 --> 00:09:08.436
Well. he's also claiming that

247
00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.655
the two of them were engaged.

248
00:09:09.698 --> 00:09:11.265
so that would explain
his fingerprints

249
00:09:11.396 --> 00:09:12.832
all over Susan's house.

250
00:09:12.919 --> 00:09:14.921
Yeah. yeah. yeah.
but that engagement ring.

251
00:09:15.008 --> 00:09:15.922
that seems to be missing.

252
00:09:16.009 --> 00:09:17.315
Hmm.

253
00:09:17.402 --> 00:09:18.881
So what. you're saying that this

254
00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:20.274
could be a robbery after all.

255
00:09:20.361 --> 00:09:21.144
and Susan was killed
over a ring?

256
00:09:21.232 --> 00:09:22.276
It's possible. right?

257
00:09:22.363 --> 00:09:23.843
Oh. yeah.

258
00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.106
I looked into vintage rings
like this for Nina.

259
00:09:26.193 --> 00:09:29.675
and a rock like that
from the '20s. good clarity.

260
00:09:29.718 --> 00:09:32.243
thing would go for 750K easy.

261
00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:34.288
- Thanks. Elise.
Well. you win.

262
00:09:34.375 --> 00:09:36.203
but by "Price is Right" rules.

263
00:09:36.334 --> 00:09:39.467
Jeremy's insurance policy puts
