a suspected front

522
00:18:53.716 --> 00:18:56.110
for the New York clan of Bratva.

523
00:18:56.241 --> 00:18:58.199
You're kidding.

524
00:18:58.286 --> 00:19:01.246
This kid accidentally stole
from the Russian mob.

525
00:19:07.295 --> 00:19:08.993
In an absolutely banner
stroke of bad luck.

526
00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:12.126
18-year-old Lucas Williams
unknowingly stole $315.000

527
00:19:12.257 --> 00:19:15.173
from Bratva. the Russian mob.

528
00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:17.305
How did they even know
Lucas was stealing from them?

529
00:19:17.436 --> 00:19:18.654
Yeah. that's... that's
nagging at me too.

530
00:19:18.785 --> 00:19:20.395
We're just getting
into it. so...

531
00:19:20.482 --> 00:19:22.006
We just arrested the boss

532
00:19:22.136 --> 00:19:23.355
of the New York clan
six months ago.

533
00:19:23.442 --> 00:19:24.356
Do we know who is in charge now?

534
00:19:24.443 --> 00:19:25.705
Uh. yeah.

535
00:19:25.792 --> 00:19:27.098
Uh. Elise. how we doing on that?

536
00:19:27.185 --> 00:19:29.361
Uh. yeah. Organized Crime
believe the new head

537
00:19:29.491 --> 00:19:32.320
of the New York clan of Bratva
to be this man.

538
00:19:32.407 --> 00:19:34.192
54 years old. named...

539
00:19:34.279 --> 00:19:35.671
Andrei Ovechkin?

540
00:19:35.802 --> 00:19:36.890
[suspenseful music]

541
00:19:37.021 --> 00:19:38.500
How long has he been
in New York?

542
00:19:38.544 --> 00:19:39.762
Immigration says three months.

543
00:19:39.893 --> 00:19:41.155
I'm guessing
you've heard of him?

544
00:19:41.242 --> 00:19:43.070
[sighs] You could say that.

545
00:19:45.681 --> 00:19:48.336
All right. so. uh.

546
00:19:48.467 --> 00:19:49.598
you remember my old man

547
00:19:49.685 --> 00:19:50.991
used to work for
the State Department. right?

548
00:19:51.078 --> 00:19:52.775
Right.

549
00:19:52.906 --> 00:19:54.516
So he was stationed in Moscow

550
00:19:54.603 --> 00:19:56.127
for a couple years
when I was 12.

551
00:19:56.214 --> 00:19:57.606
I went to the international
school over there.

552
00:19:57.693 --> 00:19:59.870
You wanna take a wild guess
who my best friend was?

553
00:20:02.046 --> 00:20:03.699
Oof.

554
00:20:03.786 --> 00:20:05.963
You were only in Moscow
for two years.

555
00:20:06.093 --> 00:20:07.703
- Yeah.
Yeah. but you know.

556
00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.923
Andrei was. you know...

557
00:20:10.054 --> 00:20:11.707
he was like a brother.

558
00:20:11.794 --> 00:20:14.145
Even after my family
moved back to the States.

559
00:20:14.232 --> 00:20:16.147
you know. we talked
as much as we could.

560
00:20:16.277 --> 00:20:17.583
We had a whole plan. you know.

561
00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:19.628
He was gonna move here.
He was gonna stay with me.

562
00:20:19.759 --> 00:20:21.717
We were gonna open up a...
[chuckles]

563
00:20:21.804 --> 00:20:22.980
Private investigator business.

564
00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.285
you know. get answers

565
00:20:24.372 --> 00:20:27.810
for people left behind
in the system.

566
00:20:27.898 --> 00:20:31.945
I smuggled a VHS tape
of "Chinatown" into Moscow.

567
00:20:32.032 --> 00:20:34.078
and we used to watch it
all the time.

568
00:20:34.165 --> 00:20:37.908
I kind of had a thing
for '70s noir.

569
00:20:37.995 --> 00:20:39.431
You still in contact with him?

570
00:20:39.561 --> 00:20:42.738
No. I haven't talked to him
since I was 20.

571
00:20:42.825 --> 00:20:44.740
The Soviet Union collapsed.

572
00:20:44.871 --> 00:20:46.307
You know. it was chaos.

573
00:20:46.394 --> 00:20:47.874
He went dark.

574
00:20:48.005 --> 00:20:50.790
Eventually. I found out he
had joined Bratva to survive.

575
00:20:50.877 --> 00:20:52.792
But his name hasn't
popped up in years.

576
00:20:52.879 --> 00:20:54.663
I figured. you know.
he had been killed

577
00:20:54.794 --> 00:20:57.101
with the trajectory he was on.

578
00:20:57.231 --> 00:21:00.974
[sighs] Seems he got
his stars instead.

579
00:21:01.061 --> 00:21:03.759
Well. his tenure as boss
will be short-lived.

580
00:21:03.846 --> 00:21:07.198
I want a full-scale raid
on his base of operations.

581
00:21:07.285 --> 00:21:08.851
We'll force his hand
to give up the girl.

582
00:21:08.895 --> 00:21:11.898
Respectfully. obviously.
Bratva is good for this.

583
00:21:11.985 --> 00:21:14.901
But with Andrei.

584
00:21:15.032 --> 00:21:16.163
if they sent him here
from Moscow.

585
00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.905
he means something
to the organization.

586
00:21:18.992 --> 00:21:20.820
and the powers that be are
watching. and he knows that.

587
00:21:20.907 --> 00:21:23.040
All the more reason
for him to make a statement.

588
00:21:23.127 --> 00:21:26.347
No one steals from Bratva
on Andrei Ovechkin's watch.

589
00:21:26.434 --> 00:21:28.045
I don't know.
my gut is just telling me

590
00:21:28.132 --> 00:21:30.264
that's not how he'd handle this.

591
00:21:30.351 --> 00:21:34.399
You know. it's sloppy.
and he's anything but sloppy.

592
00:21:34.486 --> 00:21:37.184
Jubal. an innocent girl's
life is on the line here.

593
00:21:37.271 --> 00:21:39.230
We've gotta have more
than just your gut.

594
00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.580
[apprehensive music]

595
00:21:41.667 --> 00:21:44.017
Are you sure you can
be objective here?

596
00:21:44.104 --> 00:21:45.801
- Oh. yeah. yeah. yeah.
No. no. no.

597
00:21:45.888 --> 00:21:49.283
No. my historical knowledge
of Andrei isn't a blind spot.

598
00:21:49.414 --> 00:21:51.851
If anything. it's an asset.

599
00:21:51.938 --> 00:21:54.114
Okay.

600
00:21:54.201 --> 00:21:56.856
How do you feel about paying
an old friend a visit?

601
00:21:56.987 --> 00:22:03.950
♪ ♪

602
00:22:08.476 --> 00:22:12.176
Hi. I'm here
to speak with Andrei.

603
00:22:12.263 --> 00:22:14.265
He's not taking visitors.

604
00:22:16.136 --> 00:22:18.660
[speaking Russian]

605
00:22:18.704 --> 00:22:21.489
[speaking Russian]

606
00:22:28.714 --> 00:22:31.717
[speaking Russian]

607
00:22:35.503 --> 00:22:38.158
That's not how we treat
our friends. is it. Mitya?

608
00:22:43.990 --> 00:22:45.513
Jubal Valentine.
[laughs]

609
00:22:45.644 --> 00:22:47.559
[chuckles]
- All right.

610
00:22:47.689 --> 00:22:51.345
Or I should say. Assistant
Special Agent in Charge. hmm?

611
00:22:51.476 --> 00:22:53.565
- Oh. okay. Yeah.
So you looked me up.

612
00:22:53.652 --> 00:22:57.264
I... I'd be surprised if you had
recognized me that fast.

613
00:22:57.351 --> 00:23:00.006
Your Russian accent
is also memorable.

614
00:23:00.093 --> 00:23:01.442
Okay.

615
00:23:01.529 --> 00:23:02.748
Come.

616
00:23:02.791 --> 00:23:03.488
We have much to discuss.

617
00:23:03.575 --> 00:23:05.098
Yeah.

618
00:23:06.752 --> 00:23:08.449
No clothes.
no weapons. no wires.

619
00:23:08.536 --> 00:23:09.581
If I didn't know any better.

620
00:23:09.711 --> 00:23:11.061
I'd say you don't trust me.
Andrei.

621
00:23:11.148 --> 00:23:14.934
The boy I knew.

622
00:23:15.021 --> 00:23:19.025
the one who referred
to the rules as suggestions.

623
00:23:19.112 --> 00:23:23.638
him. I trusted with my life.

624
00:23:23.769 --> 00:23:25.075
You disappeared on me. man.

625
00:23:25.162 --> 00:23:26.163
[laughs]

626
00:23:26.293 --> 00:23:28.556
What happened. right?

627
00:23:28.687 --> 00:23:31.429
[sighs] Jubal.

628
00:23:31.516 --> 00:23:32.865
please.

629
00:23:32.952 --> 00:23:34.954
[apprehensive music]

630
00:23:35.041 --> 00:23:38.349
I'm not so naive to think
this is a social call.

631
00:23:39.306 --> 00:23:41.221
Yeah. Well. you're right.

632
00:23:41.352 --> 00:23:43.615
Did your men abduct
a 15-year-old girl

633
00:23:43.658 --> 00:23:45.138
named Faith Williams yesterday?

634
00:23:45.225 --> 00:23:47.227
We did not.

635
00:23:47.271 --> 00:23:50.665
I know about
the stolen crypto wallet

636
00:23:50.796 --> 00:23:53.103
that belonged
to the Bratva front.

637
00:23:53.190 --> 00:23:55.801
And you guys have no sympathy
for thieves.

638
00:23:55.844 --> 00:23:59.674
So I am speaking to the FBI.

639
00:23:59.761 --> 00:24:01.763
not my old friend.

640
00:24:03.809 --> 00:24:05.724
We both made choices.

641
00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:12.252
Yeah. we were out some Bitcoin.

642
00:24:12.383 --> 00:24:14.559
but I don't play games
for small prices.

643
00:24:14.646 --> 00:24:16.430
315K. that's not nothing.

644
00:24:16.474 --> 00:24:18.780
To us? Please.

645
00:24:18.867 --> 00:24:21.827
And look at the trouble
it's caused between the FBI.

646
00:24:21.870 --> 00:24:23.089
the online exposure.

647
00:24:23.176 --> 00:24:24.221
Online exposure?

648
00:24:24.308 --> 00:24:27.615
Bratva's shame is now public.

649
00:24:27.702 --> 00:24:30.183
Everyone know
that boy stole from us.

650
00:24:30.270 --> 00:24:32.751
His name.
his address. the amount...

651
00:24:32.838 --> 00:24:34.883
it's all posted online.

652
00:24:35.014 --> 00:24:36.537
So this kid made a fool of you.

653
00:24:36.668 --> 00:24:38.670
and you knew exactly who he was
and where you could find him.

654
00:24:38.757 --> 00:24:42.717
Jubal. anyone knows how much
cash that boy is sitting on.

655
00:24:42.804 --> 00:24:45.720
Why would I do that?

656
00:24:45.851 --> 00:24:48.854
I knew it's gonna be
open season on the boy.

657
00:24:48.984 --> 00:24:51.291
♪ ♪

658
00:24:51.378 --> 00:24:53.293
Andrei was telling you
the truth.

659
00:24:53.380 --> 00:24:55.165
The forum is called
Protect the Block.

660
00:24:55.252 --> 00:24:57.515
referring to the block chain.

661
00:24:57.645 --> 00:24:58.690
So Lucas Williams was doxxed
on this forum.

662
00:24:58.777 --> 00:25:00.387
He was.

663
00:25:00.518 --> 00:25:02.302
The site tracks suspicious
crypto transactions...

664
00:25:02.433 --> 00:25:05.740
anonymously. but I am
working on ID'ing them.

665
00:25:05.827 --> 00:25:07.960
And Cyber Crimes had no idea
about this forum?

666
00:25:08.090 --> 00:25:09.744
We don't have the manpower.

667
00:25:09.875 --> 00:25:12.747
Crypto theft is
the Wild West of cybercrime.

668
00:25:12.878 --> 00:25:14.314
Fitting 'cause
whoever runs this forum

669
00:25:14.401 --> 00:25:16.098
claims to be a white hat hacker.

670
00:25:16.186 --> 00:25:19.624
But this hacker.
he. what. deputized himself?

671
00:25:19.711 --> 00:25:21.495
He thinks they're on
the side of justice.

672
00:25:21.626 --> 00:25:23.671
Yes. if they suspect someone
has stolen Bitcoin

673
00:25:23.758 --> 00:25:26.239
from another wallet.
they expose the thief.

674
00:25:26.326 --> 00:25:29.590
Tagline of the forum is.
"Actions have consequences."

675
00:25:29.721 --> 00:25:32.332
Right. a-and they flagged
Lucas Williams's scam.

676
00:25:32.463 --> 00:25:34.856
posted his address.
photos. all that.

677
00:25:34.943 --> 00:25:36.467
And the exact amount
that he stole.

678
00:25:36.597 --> 00:25:38.077
Okay.

679
00:25:38.164 --> 00:25:40.601
Well. that's an
"X marks the spot"

680
00:25:40.688 --> 00:25:43.648
for any criminal who wants to
grab 315.000 in stolen crypto.

681
00:25:43.735 --> 00:25:45.737
And anyone with an internet
connection can see it.

682
00:25:45.867 --> 00:25:47.129
I guess that's what Andrei meant

683
00:25:47.217 --> 00:25:49.654
when he said it's open season.

684
00:25:49.741 --> 00:25:51.569
I just unmasked our white hat...

685
00:25:51.699 --> 00:25:54.920
Whitney Kabialis. software
developer here in the city.

686
00:25:55.007 --> 00:25:56.878
She might know more.

687
00:25:56.965 --> 00:25:57.705
[door buzzes]

688
00:26:00.491 --> 00:26:01.927
I did nothing wrong.

689
00:26:02.014 --> 00:26:04.321
Doxxing isn't even a crime.

690
00:26:04.364 --> 00:26:05.713
That kid stole the money.

691
00:26:05.800 --> 00:26:07.367
I just caught him
before you did.

692
00:26:07.454 --> 00:26:09.456
No. Whitney. what you did

693
00:26:09.543 --> 00:26:11.502
was set off
a chain of criminal events

694
00:26:11.589 --> 00:26:15.462
that led to two people
being murdered.

695
00:26:15.593 --> 00:26:18.248
including the abduction
of an innocent girl.

696
00:26:19.640 --> 00:26:21.773
Faith Williams is 15.

697
00:26:21.903 --> 00:26:23.253
She had nothing to do with this.

698
00:26:23.340 --> 00:26:25.167
and now her life
is being ransomed

699
00:26:25.211 --> 00:26:28.301
for some stolen Bitcoin.
all thanks to your forum.

700
00:26:28.388 --> 00:26:30.956
- I hope you find the girl.
I really do.

701
00:26:31.043 --> 00:26:33.654
But I am not responsible for
what nutjobs do with my posts.

702
00:26:33.741 --> 00:26:36.091
Legally. that is not true.

703
00:26:36.178 --> 00:26:38.529
You will be charged
with accessory to murder.

704
00:26:38.572 --> 00:26:41.271
kidnapping.
endangerment of a minor.

705
00:26:41.358 --> 00:26:43.925
What is it that you always say?

706
00:26:44.012 --> 00:26:45.623
"Actions have consequences"?

707
00:26:45.710 --> 00:26:46.798
[tense music]

708
00:26:46.928 --> 00:26:48.408
[door buzzes]

709
00:26:48.495 --> 00:26:50.715
- Now a good time?
- It's perfect.

710
00:26:50.802 --> 00:26:52.064
Whitney here was
just about to offer

711
00:26:52.151 --> 00:26:54.066
her full cooperation. right?

712
00:26:54.153 --> 00:26:56.808
Yeah. I'll help.

713
00:26:56.895 --> 00:26:58.331
Terrific.

714
00:26:58.375 --> 00:27:02.204
Meet FBI intelligence
analyst Ian Lim.

715
00:27:02.292 --> 00:27:05.077
He's the one who cracked
your forum security

716
00:27:05.207 --> 00:27:07.645
and identified you.
- Shadow proxy?

717
00:27:07.732 --> 00:27:09.995
Been trying to narrow down
who might have seen your post

718
00:27:10.038 --> 00:27:11.953
with Lucas Williams'
information.

719
00:27:12.040 --> 00:27:14.086
but your site wipes
all incoming IP addresses.

720
00:27:14.173 --> 00:27:17.481
- Yeah. volatile logging.
There is no backup.

721
00:27:17.524 --> 00:27:19.526
You must have the kidnappers'
wallet address. right?

722
00:27:19.613 --> 00:27:21.223
Yes. it was included
in the ransom.

723
00:27:21.267 --> 00:27:24.270
You should be able to ID them
from the previous transactions.

724
00:27:24.357 --> 00:27:26.881
New wallet. never been used.

725
00:27:26.968 --> 00:27:28.405
So they know what they're doing.

726
00:27:28.535 --> 00:27:30.058
What haven't I tried?

727
00:27:30.145 --> 00:27:32.583
We have no other way to track
or even communicate with them.

728
00:27:32.713 --> 00:27:35.281
♪ ♪

729
00:27:35.368 --> 00:27:36.804
This girl's life depends on it.

730
00:27:36.935 --> 00:27:40.417
♪ ♪

731
00:27:40.504 --> 00:27:41.722
Sending crypto is
the only real way

732
00:27:41.809 --> 00:27:43.420
to elicit wallet activity.

733
00:27:43.463 --> 00:27:45.117
Wait. I...

734
00:27:45.204 --> 00:27:46.423
sorry.
I'm trying to keep up here.

735
00:27:46.510 --> 00:27:48.163
It sounds like you're saying
the only way

736
00:27:48.250 --> 00:27:50.427
to trace back to the kidnappers

737
00:27:50.514 --> 00:27:52.907
is to actually send the Bitcoin.

738
00:27:53.038 --> 00:27:54.866
Unless...

739
00:27:54.953 --> 00:27:57.869
we drop something else
in their wallet.

740
00:27:57.956 --> 00:28:02.482
♪ ♪

741
00:28:02.526 --> 00:28:04.397
All right. I know I'm still
out here carrying cash.

742
00:28:04.484 --> 00:28:06.225
but I think I understand
enough about crypto

743
00:28:06.312 --> 00:28:09.359
to know you can't send a text
to a wallet address. right?

744
00:28:09.446 --> 00:28:11.317
- Correct.
You can only send crypto.

745
00:28:11.404 --> 00:28:14.407
But I can create
a new digital coin

746
00:28:14.494 --> 00:28:16.104
that we can send
to the kidnappers' wallet.

747
00:28:16.235 --> 00:28:18.933
What. you can just create
a new cryptocurrency?

748
00:28:19.064 --> 00:28:20.718
- Anyone can.
It takes five minutes.

749
00:28:20.805 --> 00:28:22.284
You're out here
printing money. bro.

750
00:28:22.415 --> 00:28:23.503
Yeah. not really.

751
00:28:23.590 --> 00:28:25.679
It'll be valueless.

752
00:28:25.766 --> 00:28:30.031
Just need it to get
the kidnappers' attention.

753
00:28:30.118 --> 00:28:32.164
May I present...

754
00:28:32.251 --> 00:28:34.688
Huh. "Proof of Life First" Coin.

755
00:28:34.732 --> 00:28:35.907
Very smart.

756
00:28:35.950 --> 00:28:37.474
The coin is the message.

757
00:28:37.561 --> 00:28:39.737
and hopefully this will get
them to turn on their burner.

758
00:28:39.824 --> 00:28:41.391
Exactly.

759
00:28:41.521 --> 00:28:43.741
As soon as this coin appears
in the kidnappers' wallet.

760
00:28:43.828 --> 00:28:45.917
it'll tell them
that Lucas is only willing

761
00:28:46.004 --> 00:28:48.136
to pay the ransom
if they prove that his sister

762
00:28:48.223 --> 00:28:49.747
is still alive.

763
00:28:49.877 --> 00:28:51.705
They turn on their burner
to send proof.

764
00:28:51.836 --> 00:28:53.403
So send it.

765
00:28:59.278 --> 00:29:00.497
Kidnappers must have seen
Ian's "Proof of Life" Coin

766
00:29:00.627 --> 00:29:01.889
and turned their
burners back on.

767
00:29:01.976 --> 00:29:03.151
Just in time.

768
00:29:03.238 --> 00:29:04.239
It looks like they
are about to respond.

769
00:29:04.283 --> 00:29:06.111
Okay. here we go.

770
00:29:06.198 --> 00:29:07.852
Lucas.
please give them the money.

771
00:29:07.939 --> 00:29:09.419
They said they're gonna kill me

772
00:29:09.506 --> 00:29:10.550
if you don't give them
the money.

773
00:29:10.681 --> 00:29:11.943
Okay. time stamp
on that news clip

774
00:29:12.073 --> 00:29:12.944
is from one minute ago.

775
00:29:13.074 --> 00:29:14.554
Turn that station on.

776
00:29:14.685 --> 00:29:16.687
[suspenseful music]

777
00:29:16.774 --> 00:29:18.776
Is that... yeah.

778
00:29:18.863 --> 00:29:21.082
- Yeah. that's live.
We can still save this girl.

779
00:29:21.169 --> 00:29:22.997
Okay. so where are
they holding her?

780
00:29:23.084 --> 00:29:25.913
The burner that they're using
doesn't have GPS services on.

781
00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:28.786
and they stripped all location
metadata from the video.

782
00:29:28.916 --> 00:29:30.788
She's in a pretty
nondescript room.

783
00:29:30.875 --> 00:29:31.963
Hang on.

784
00:29:32.050 --> 00:29:34.052
That structure

785
00:29:34.139 --> 00:29:37.751
is a round masonry heater.

786
00:29:37.838 --> 00:29:39.100
Uh. that kind of brick design
with a small firebox.

787
00:29:39.187 --> 00:29:40.450
that's really unusual.

788
00:29:40.537 --> 00:29:42.103
It's German style.

789
00:29:42.190 --> 00:29:44.454
circa 1900 to 1915.

790
00:29:44.584 --> 00:29:46.760
You're up on 20th century
masonry now. Moran?

791
00:29:46.847 --> 00:29:48.240
I helped my uncle renovate
a building one summer.

792
00:29:48.327 --> 00:29:49.807
Would you let the man cook?

793
00:29:49.850 --> 00:29:51.983
Most owners ripped
these out by the '90s

794
00:29:52.113 --> 00:29:54.681
because of the city's updated
Air Pollution Control Code.

795
00:29:54.768 --> 00:29:57.292
but the ones that didn't
need to file permits.

796
00:29:57.336 --> 00:29:58.903
Elise.
- Yeah.

797
00:29:58.990 --> 00:30:00.905
There can't be many
of those things left.

798
00:30:01.035 --> 00:30:04.386
Searching Department of
Buildings records for Section...

799
00:30:04.474 --> 00:30:05.910
- 21.
- 21 masonry permits.

800
00:30:05.997 --> 00:30:09.827
filtering by year and style.

801
00:30:09.957 --> 00:30:11.176
Okay.
And then there were four left.

802
00:30:11.219 --> 00:30:12.394
Yeah. we'll split the team.

803
00:30:12.482 --> 00:30:14.179
We'll narrow it down
on the ground.

804
00:30:14.309 --> 00:30:21.273
♪ ♪

805
00:30:21.403 --> 00:30:23.884
Okay. SWAT's still
a few minutes out.

806
00:30:24.015 --> 00:30:26.104
Maggie and OA cleared
the other two buildings.

807
00:30:26.191 --> 00:30:28.367
So you've got a 50/50 shot
with this one.

808
00:30:28.454 --> 00:30:29.716
Just proceed with caution.

809
00:30:29.803 --> 00:30:35.635
♪ ♪

810
00:30:35.722 --> 00:30:38.029
We're in the right place.

811
00:30:38.116 --> 00:30:39.900
Confirmed. Jubal. this is
where Faith was being held.

812
00:30:39.987 --> 00:30:42.207
Copy that.

813
00:30:42.250 --> 00:30:43.643
[indistinct Russian chatter]

814
00:30:43.730 --> 00:30:45.776
- It's almost time.
We gotta go.

815
00:30:45.906 --> 00:30:50.650
♪ ♪

816
00:30:50.737 --> 00:30:52.783
- All right. I count two...
armed.

817
00:30:52.870 --> 00:30:54.567
Any eyes on Faith?
- Negative.

818
00:30:54.611 --> 00:30:57.352
We gotta confirm
that Faith is on site.

819
00:30:57.396 --> 00:30:58.789
Copy. Going right.

820
00:30:58.919 --> 00:31:04.882
♪ ♪

821
00:31:06.797 --> 00:31:08.146
[gunshots]

822
00:31:08.233 --> 00:31:09.582
Go. go. go.

823
00:31:09.626 --> 00:31:11.236
[gunshots]

824
00:31:14.282 --> 00:31:16.284
- Got him?
- Go!

825
00:31:16.371 --> 00:31:19.244
[intense music]

826
00:31:19.374 --> 00:31:23.161
♪ ♪

827
00:31:23.248 --> 00:31:24.292
[buzzer blares]

828
00:31:24.379 --> 00:31:31.473
♪ ♪

829
00:31:39.394 --> 00:31:40.961
[tires squeal. engine revving]

830
00:31:41.092 --> 00:31:43.660
OpCen. two male suspects
fleeing north on DuPont.

831
00:31:43.747 --> 00:31:46.053
black Dodge Challenger.
Couldn't get a plate.

832
00:31:46.097 --> 00:31:48.142
Put out a BOLO now.

833
00:31:48.229 --> 00:31:50.101
So... so two kidnappers
got away.

834
00:31:50.231 --> 00:31:51.363
One was killed.

835
00:31:51.493 --> 00:31:52.669
What about
Lucas Williams's sister?

836
00:31:52.756 --> 00:31:53.713
No. Eva and Scola
swept the property.

837
00:31:53.844 --> 00:31:54.888
She was not there.

838
00:31:55.019 --> 00:31:56.150
So we don't know
if she's alive or dead.

839
00:31:56.281 --> 00:31:57.369
No. but we're
digging into the perp

840
00:31:57.456 --> 00:31:58.500
that our team took down.
How we doing. Elise?

841
00:31:58.588 --> 00:32:00.807
Yep. Simon Brumel. 20 years old.

842
00:32:00.894 --> 00:32:03.549
No gang affiliation.
just minor drug possession.

843
00:32:03.593 --> 00:32:05.290
assault charges
for a couple bar fights.

844
00:32:05.377 --> 00:32:06.900
It's a big leap
from drunk and disorderly

845
00:32:06.987 --> 00:32:09.076
to murder and kidnapping.
- Got something.

846
00:32:09.163 --> 00:32:14.081
Simon wasn't affiliated.
but looks like his father was.

847
00:32:15.387 --> 00:32:16.736
He's Bratva?

848
00:32:16.867 --> 00:32:23.221
♪ ♪

849
00:32:23.308 --> 00:32:24.352
Why are you sweating. man?

850
00:32:24.439 --> 00:32:25.876
We'll be there.

851
00:32:28.182 --> 00:32:30.924
- You lied to me.
- Go to another room.

852
00:32:31.011 --> 00:32:33.753
Faith Williams' kidnappers.
they... they work for you.

853
00:32:33.840 --> 00:32:35.407
You really thought
I wouldn't figure it out?

854
00:32:35.537 --> 00:32:36.451
You're not that slick.

855
00:32:36.538 --> 00:32:37.844
Do not mistake our history

856
00:32:37.931 --> 00:32:40.151
for permission to disrespect me.

857
00:32:40.281 --> 00:32:42.370
I'm starting to question
our history altogether.

858
00:32:42.501 --> 00:32:44.242
What are you doing. man?
She is a child.

859
00:32:44.329 --> 00:32:45.983
I did not order this.

860
00:32:46.113 --> 00:32:48.072
- No?
We ID'd one of the kidnappers.

861
00:32:48.159 --> 00:32:50.552
The name Brumel ring any bells?

862
00:32:50.683 --> 00:32:52.642
Brumel's boy does not
work for me.

863
00:32:52.729 --> 00:32:54.513
None of those kids do.

864
00:32:54.644 --> 00:32:57.298
I heard whispers
about these kids.

865
00:32:57.385 --> 00:33:00.911
they're trying to make
a reputation. to get noticed.

866
00:33:00.954 --> 00:33:05.263
Well. they did. just not
so much how they hoped.

867
00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:08.875
And I found out
only after you came here.

868
00:33:10.224 --> 00:33:12.444
I don't know where
they're holding the girl.

869
00:33:12.531 --> 00:33:14.011
♪ ♪

870
00:33:14.098 --> 00:33:16.187
Prove it.

871
00:33:16.317 --> 00:33:17.405
Help me save her.

872
00:33:17.492 --> 00:33:22.846
♪ ♪

873
00:33:27.546 --> 00:33:30.070
[tense music]

874
00:33:30.114 --> 00:33:30.854
Thank you.

875
00:33:33.508 --> 00:33:36.076
Thank you. Robin.

876
00:33:36.120 --> 00:33:37.991
[sighs] You want some?

877
00:33:38.078 --> 00:33:41.081
Still eating like
a 14-year-old. I see.

878
00:33:41.125 --> 00:33:44.084
Old habits. I know.

879
00:33:44.128 --> 00:33:45.869
It'll be the death of me.

880
00:33:45.956 --> 00:33:46.739
[chuckles]

881
00:33:49.655 --> 00:33:53.354
Trust. Jubal.

882
00:33:53.441 --> 00:33:55.574
I asked these kids to meet.

883
00:33:55.661 --> 00:33:56.836
They'll come to me.

884
00:33:59.012 --> 00:34:01.493
Andrei's intel helped us
identify these two men

885
00:34:01.623 --> 00:34:02.799
as our kidnappers...

886
00:34:02.886 --> 00:34:06.019
Nikita Kharkov and Ilia Marinov.

887
00:34:06.106 --> 00:34:07.716
They're practically kids.

888
00:34:07.760 --> 00:34:10.370
If they spook and they
don't show up. we have nothing.

889
00:34:10.457 --> 00:34:12.417
Having a face-to-face
with Andrei means something.

890
00:34:12.504 --> 00:34:13.678
If they're trying to move up.
this is their chance

891
00:34:13.765 --> 00:34:15.681
to impress the boss.

892
00:34:15.768 --> 00:34:17.204
They think recovering
Andrei's 300K

893
00:34:17.291 --> 00:34:19.466
will make them invaluable
to Bratva.

894
00:34:19.553 --> 00:34:21.207
Okay. Jubal's wire is hot.

895
00:34:21.294 --> 00:34:23.689
He and Andrei are gonna get
them to incriminate themselves.

896
00:34:23.776 --> 00:34:25.734
then we will arrest them
and use that information

897
00:34:25.778 --> 00:34:27.867
to see if we can get
Faith Williams' location.

898
00:34:27.954 --> 00:34:29.564
Andrei could have
something planned here.

899
00:34:29.608 --> 00:34:31.131
Are we sure we trust him?

900
00:34:31.262 --> 00:34:31.957
No.

901
00:34:34.178 --> 00:34:35.788
Oh. showtime.

902
00:34:35.919 --> 00:34:37.616
Hey. Jubal.
we have a car pulling up now.

903
00:34:37.747 --> 00:34:40.227
Is it the black Dodge we
last saw the suspects driving?

904
00:34:40.314 --> 00:34:43.013
No. it's a green BMW.

905
00:34:45.189 --> 00:34:46.406
Okay. we got a problem.

906
00:34:46.538 --> 00:34:49.106
Nikita's the only one
that showed up.

907
00:34:49.193 --> 00:34:50.498
That means that Ilia
might be with Faith

908
00:34:50.629 --> 00:34:52.109
at a different location.

909
00:34:52.152 --> 00:34:53.457
I think it's gonna put her
in danger

910
00:34:53.544 --> 00:34:54.763
if we arrest Nikita here.

911
00:34:54.850 --> 00:34:56.591
What I think you should do
is get Nikita

912
00:34:56.722 --> 00:34:58.115
to say the location
where they're holding Faith.

913
00:34:58.202 --> 00:35:00.378
And whatever you do.
make sure that Nikita

914
00:35:00.508 --> 00:35:01.771
and Ilia don't speak.

915
00:35:01.901 --> 00:35:04.730
♪ ♪

916
00:35:04.817 --> 00:35:05.644
- Here he comes.
[clears throat]

917
00:35:05.731 --> 00:35:08.125
Mm. Mm-hmm. Da. Da.

918
00:35:08.255 --> 00:35:15.045
♪ ♪

919
00:35:16.524 --> 00:35:18.439
You wanted my attention.

920
00:35:18.526 --> 00:35:19.701
You have it.

921
00:35:36.544 --> 00:35:38.546
We figured out who robbed you.

922
00:35:38.633 --> 00:35:41.462
Did I ask you to do that?

923
00:35:41.549 --> 00:35:43.203
Do I know you at all?

924
00:35:43.334 --> 00:35:44.552
No.

925
00:35:47.381 --> 00:35:50.123
But I know you.

926
00:35:50.210 --> 00:35:51.472
I could be an asset to you.

927
00:35:51.559 --> 00:35:54.345
Make sure no one steals
from you ever again.

928
00:35:54.432 --> 00:35:55.781
So where's my money?

929
00:35:58.436 --> 00:36:02.222
I'll have it in...

930
00:36:02.309 --> 00:36:04.485
90 seconds.

931
00:36:04.572 --> 00:36:06.357
How... how much?

932
00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:08.272
All of it.

933
00:36:08.402 --> 00:36:11.536
315.000 in Bitcoin.

934
00:36:11.623 --> 00:36:14.321
Is it me. or are you also
feeling a little doubtful here?

935
00:36:14.408 --> 00:36:16.280
I mean. why is this...
why is he so confident

936
00:36:16.367 --> 00:36:18.064
that the money's
gonna come through?

937
00:36:18.195 --> 00:36:20.937
[speaking Russian]

938
00:36:22.416 --> 00:36:23.983
I'm the accountant. Okay?

939
00:36:24.027 --> 00:36:27.857
He is part of Bratva.
unlike you.

940
00:36:27.987 --> 00:36:29.902
Answer his question.

941
00:36:31.643 --> 00:36:35.038
We're not stupid. okay?

942
00:36:35.168 --> 00:36:37.257
We have the sister
as collateral.

943
00:36:37.388 --> 00:36:39.825
You don't get your money
by 5:00 p.m.. we kill her.

944
00:36:39.912 --> 00:36:43.481
Okay. well. I hate to break
it to you. but it's 5:00 p.m..

945
00:36:43.611 --> 00:36:45.265
so where is it?

946
00:36:45.396 --> 00:36:46.353
I see no money.

947
00:36:46.440 --> 00:36:53.404
♪ ♪

948
00:36:53.491 --> 00:36:56.059
[sighs] We'll show
the thief we're serious.

949
00:36:56.189 --> 00:36:57.843
Ilia will finish the job.
- No. no. no.

950
00:36:57.930 --> 00:36:59.976
No. no. stop. stop. stop. stop.

951
00:37:00.063 --> 00:37:01.760
You kill that girl.
my boss doesn't

952
00:37:01.847 --> 00:37:03.022
get his money. all right?

953
00:37:03.066 --> 00:37:04.676
You need to tell us
where she is.

954
00:37:06.547 --> 00:37:08.158
Hey. I said stop.

955
00:37:08.201 --> 00:37:09.333
You need to tell us
where the girl is right now.

956
00:37:09.463 --> 00:37:11.901
- Let go of me!
I can handle this. okay?

957
00:37:11.944 --> 00:37:13.859
[slams table] Enough.

958
00:37:13.946 --> 00:37:16.427
Tell me where the girl is
before your stupidity

959
00:37:16.514 --> 00:37:18.472
brings us all down.

960
00:37:18.516 --> 00:37:21.171
The real men will
clean up your mess.

961
00:37:23.129 --> 00:37:26.785
You're gonna wanna check
how you talk to me. old man.

962
00:37:26.916 --> 00:37:28.134
I'll be running Bratva one day.

963
00:37:28.221 --> 00:37:31.050
Kid...

964
00:37:31.137 --> 00:37:34.358
you will never be a part
of my organization.

965
00:37:34.488 --> 00:37:37.361
♪ ♪

966
00:37:37.448 --> 00:37:38.362
[grunts]

967
00:37:38.449 --> 00:37:39.363
Damn it.

968
00:37:39.450 --> 00:37:40.799
[scream]

969
00:37:40.886 --> 00:37:42.496
[grunting]

970
00:37:42.583 --> 00:37:44.890
[clattering]

971
00:37:44.977 --> 00:37:46.892
- FBI.
- Let me see. Let me see.

972
00:37:46.936 --> 00:37:49.025
We need a medic in here!

973
00:37:49.112 --> 00:37:51.201
- It's over. Nikita.
- Get off me!

974
00:37:51.288 --> 00:37:52.550
Where is Faith Williams?

975
00:37:52.637 --> 00:37:54.291
Huh?

976
00:37:54.378 --> 00:37:56.815
You better pray that
that girl is still alive.

977
00:37:56.902 --> 00:37:59.774
Where is she. Nikita? Tell me!

978
00:37:59.818 --> 00:38:02.516
Maggie. Ilia is two blocks
north in the Dodge Challenger.

979
00:38:02.603 --> 00:38:03.691
He has Faith.

980
00:38:03.778 --> 00:38:05.432
Copy. We're on our way.

981
00:38:05.519 --> 00:38:08.087
♪ ♪

982
00:38:08.131 --> 00:38:09.480
[gunshots]

983
00:38:09.523 --> 00:38:10.611
Don't shoot.

984
00:38:10.698 --> 00:38:11.786
She's in the trunk.

985
00:38:13.919 --> 00:38:15.573
I could skip a round.

986
00:38:15.660 --> 00:38:17.053
Okay. well. don't miss.

987
00:38:17.140 --> 00:38:19.707
FBI! Drop your weapon!

988
00:38:19.794 --> 00:38:22.145
[gunshot]
- [yells]

989
00:38:22.275 --> 00:38:23.233
Go. Go. go.

990
00:38:23.320 --> 00:38:26.062
- [groaning]
- I got him.

991
00:38:30.370 --> 00:38:31.328
Hey. Faith.

992
00:38:31.371 --> 00:38:32.938
[groans]

993
00:38:33.069 --> 00:38:34.287
You're okay.

994
00:38:34.374 --> 00:38:35.723
- [whimpers]
- Hey.

995
00:38:37.551 --> 00:38:38.988
Where's Lucas?

996
00:38:39.075 --> 00:38:41.077
Where's my brother?

997
00:38:41.164 --> 00:38:42.339
I want my brother.

998
00:38:42.382 --> 00:38:43.688
- We've got him. Faith.
He's safe.

999
00:38:43.775 --> 00:38:45.298
Come on.

1000
00:38:45.385 --> 00:38:47.692
- Is he okay?
- He's okay.

1001
00:38:47.779 --> 00:38:51.435
[somber music]

1002
00:38:51.565 --> 00:38:57.441
♪ ♪

1003
00:38:57.571 --> 00:39:01.140
[crying]

1004
00:39:01.227 --> 00:39:05.231
Such a tragedy. right?

1005
00:39:05.275 --> 00:39:07.625
Kid just made one bad choice
after another.

1006
00:39:07.712 --> 00:39:10.106
He was just trying
to save his family.

1007
00:39:10.193 --> 00:39:12.064
- Dad is dead.
He's going to prison.

1008
00:39:12.151 --> 00:39:15.111
That girl is gonna end up
in foster care.

1009
00:39:15.241 --> 00:39:17.156
I wish this one
had a happier ending.

1010
00:39:17.243 --> 00:39:18.766
[sighs] Yeah. me too.

1011
00:39:18.853 --> 00:39:22.074
They are both still young.

1012
00:39:22.161 --> 00:39:25.773
You know. with early parole

1013
00:39:25.860 --> 00:39:27.340
and the right support system.

1014
00:39:27.427 --> 00:39:28.907
maybe it's not too late

1015
00:39:28.994 --> 00:39:32.737
for Lucas to make
different choices.

1016
00:39:32.824 --> 00:39:34.565
I'd like to believe that.

1017
00:39:34.652 --> 00:39:36.045
Yeah.

1018
00:39:36.175 --> 00:39:40.832
♪ ♪

1019
00:39:40.962 --> 00:39:44.879
[crying]

1020
00:39:59.416 --> 00:40:01.244
[sighs]

1021
00:40:01.331 --> 00:40:04.595
Some things never change. Jubal.

1022
00:40:04.682 --> 00:40:07.250
I can hear you
thinking from in here.

1023
00:40:07.293 --> 00:40:10.122
[chuckles]

1024
00:40:10.209 --> 00:40:12.690
I couldn't tell
if you were awake.

1025
00:40:12.733 --> 00:40:15.519
I am glad you're gonna be okay.

1026
00:40:15.606 --> 00:40:19.175
It'll take more than this
to bring me down.

1027
00:40:19.262 --> 00:40:22.395
Today was almost like
the old days.

1028
00:40:22.482 --> 00:40:24.484
That's your idea
of a good time. huh?

1029
00:40:24.571 --> 00:40:27.270
Well. speaking of the old days.

1030
00:40:27.357 --> 00:40:28.445
I brought you something.

1031
00:40:31.491 --> 00:40:34.712
Remember our little
side business in Moscow?

1032
00:40:34.799 --> 00:40:38.194
Stealing pastila
from the school comms

1033
00:40:38.281 --> 00:40:41.675
and selling it to the rich kids
at twice the price.

1034
00:40:41.719 --> 00:40:43.286
[laughs]

1035
00:40:43.373 --> 00:40:44.417
It was a nice
little scheme. huh?

1036
00:40:44.504 --> 00:40:45.549
- Yeah.
[chuckles]

1037
00:40:45.679 --> 00:40:49.727
We were always a good team.

1038
00:40:49.770 --> 00:40:51.294
Yeah. we were.

1039
00:40:53.948 --> 00:40:57.082
How long are you gonna be
in New York for. you think?

1040
00:40:57.169 --> 00:41:00.346
I'm sure someone in your
office can answer that for you.

1041
00:41:05.046 --> 00:41:06.918
It's not too late.

1042
00:41:07.048 --> 00:41:09.138
[sighs]

1043
00:41:09.225 --> 00:41:12.141
I know... I know
it wouldn't be

1044
00:41:12.271 --> 00:41:15.970
exactly how we planned. but...

1045
00:41:16.057 --> 00:41:19.322
I could help you actually

1046
00:41:19.452 --> 00:41:21.411
get out.

1047
00:41:22.760 --> 00:41:25.850
You have to work with me.
We can make it happen.

1048
00:41:27.112 --> 00:41:29.941
I know what you're saying.

1049
00:41:29.984 --> 00:41:32.900
I. too. am happy to
see you again. Jubal.

1050
00:41:33.031 --> 00:41:35.164
But...

1051
00:41:37.601 --> 00:41:39.820
[sighs]

1052
00:41:39.907 --> 00:41:44.216
Next time we meet.

1053
00:41:44.347 --> 00:41:47.741
I do not expect
it will be as friends.

1054
00:41:47.872 --> 00:41:52.659
♪ ♪

1055
00:41:52.746 --> 00:41:53.965
[sighs]

1056
00:41:54.095 --> 00:42:01.102
♪ ♪

1057
00:42:02.887 --> 00:42:05.019
Get well soon. Andrei.

1058
00:42:05.106 --> 00:42:12.201
♪ ♪

1059
00:42:18.598 --> 00:42:21.471
[dramatic music]

1060
00:42:21.601 --> 00:42:28.347
♪ ♪

1061
00:42:37.791 --> 00:42:39.445
[wolf howls]
